<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Atlantis Research Database</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0d0f14;
    --bg2: #13161e;
    --bg3: #1a1e2a;
    --border: rgba(255,255,255,0.07);
    --border2: rgba(255,255,255,0.13);
    --gold: #c9a84c;
    --gold2: #e8c87a;
    --teal: #4ecdc4;
    --coral: #e8775a;
    --muted: #6b7280;
    --text: #e2e8f0;
    --text2: #94a3b8;
    --text3: #64748b;
    --s1: #7c6af5;
    --s2: #4ecdc4;
    --s3: #e8775a;
    --c3: #22c55e;
    --c2: #eab308;
    --c1: #f97316;
    --c0: #6b7280;
    --radius: 6px;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }
  /* Header */
  header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border2);
    padding: 2rem 2.5rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg2);
  }
  .header-inner { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: normal;
    color: var(--gold2);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .subtitle {
    color: var(--text2);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
  }
  /* Controls */
  .controls {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1rem 2.5rem;
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 100;
  }
  .controls-inner {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .search-wrap { position: relative; flex: 1; min-width: 220px; }
  .search-wrap input {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--bg3);
    border: 1px solid var(--border2);
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem 0.5rem 2.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-family: inherit;
    outline: none;
  }
  .search-wrap input:focus { border-color: var(--gold); }
  .search-icon {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.6rem;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .filter-group { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .filter-btn {
    background: var(--bg3);
    border: 1px solid var(--border2);
    color: var(--text2);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 12px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .filter-btn:hover { border-color: var(--gold); color: var(--gold); }
  .filter-btn.active { background: var(--gold); color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--gold); font-weight: bold; }
  .filter-btn.src-s1.active { background: var(--s1); border-color: var(--s1); }
  .filter-btn.src-s2.active { background: var(--s2); border-color: var(--s2); color: var(--bg); }
  .filter-btn.src-s3.active { background: var(--s3); border-color: var(--s3); }
  .count-badge {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text3);
    margin-left: auto;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* Main layout */
  .main { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 2.5rem 4rem; }
  /* Category section */
  .category-section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .category-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border2);
  }
  .category-label {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .category-count {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--text3);
    background: var(--bg3);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  /* Entry card */
  .entry {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .entry:hover { border-color: var(--border2); }
  .entry.hidden { display: none; }
  .entry-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .corr-badge {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    margin-top: 1px;
  }
  .corr-3 { background: rgba(34,197,94,0.15); color: var(--c3); border: 1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.3); }
  .corr-2 { background: rgba(234,179,8,0.15); color: var(--c2); border: 1px solid rgba(234,179,8,0.3); }
  .corr-1 { background: rgba(249,115,22,0.15); color: var(--c1); border: 1px solid rgba(249,115,22,0.3); }
  .corr-0 { background: rgba(107,114,128,0.15); color: var(--c0); border: 1px solid rgba(107,114,128,0.3); }
  .entry-claim {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.5;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .entry-claim strong { color: var(--gold2); font-weight: normal; }
  /* Source pills */
  .source-pills { display: flex; gap: 0.35rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .pill {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid;
  }
  .pill-s1 { color: var(--s1); border-color: rgba(124,106,245,0.4); background: rgba(124,106,245,0.08); }
  .pill-s2 { color: var(--s2); border-color: rgba(78,205,196,0.4); background: rgba(78,205,196,0.08); }
  .pill-s3 { color: var(--s3); border-color: rgba(232,119,90,0.4); background: rgba(232,119,90,0.08); }
  .pill-div { color: var(--coral); border-color: rgba(232,119,90,0.4); background: rgba(232,119,90,0.08); }
  /* Detail rows */
  .detail-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr;
    gap: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 12px;
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .detail-label { color: var(--text3); font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; padding-top: 1px; }
  .detail-val { color: var(--text2); }
  .detail-val.conflict { color: var(--coral); }
  .detail-val.agree { color: var(--teal); }
  .note-row {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text3);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  /* Legend */
  .legend {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    background: var(--bg2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
  }
  .legend-item { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; color: var(--text3); }
  .legend-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; }
  /* No results */
  .no-results { text-align: center; padding: 3rem; color: var(--text3); font-style: italic; display: none; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="header-inner">
    <div class="eyebrow">Cross-Source Psychic Research — Atlantis Project</div>
    <h1>Atlantis Research Database</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">Sources: S1 Edgar Cayce (1923–44) · S2 Sarah Breskman Cosme (2020) · S3 Bashar / Darryl Anka (1983–present)</div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="controls">
  <div class="controls-inner">
    <div class="search-wrap">
      <span class="search-icon">⌕</span>
      <input type="text" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search claims, notes, sources..." oninput="filterEntries()">
    </div>
    <div class="filter-group">
      <button class="filter-btn active" onclick="setFilter('all', this)">All</button>
      <button class="filter-btn src-s1" onclick="setFilter('s1', this)">S1 Cayce</button>
      <button class="filter-btn src-s2" onclick="setFilter('s2', this)">S2 Cosme</button>
      <button class="filter-btn src-s3" onclick="setFilter('s3', this)">S3 Bashar</button>
    </div>
    <div class="filter-group">
      <button class="filter-btn" onclick="setCorr('all-corr', this)">All</button>
      <button class="filter-btn" onclick="setCorr('3', this)" style="color:var(--c3)">★★★</button>
      <button class="filter-btn" onclick="setCorr('2', this)" style="color:var(--c2)">★★</button>
      <button class="filter-btn" onclick="setCorr('1', this)" style="color:var(--c1)">★</button>
      <button class="filter-btn" onclick="setCorr('0', this)" style="color:var(--c0)">Unique</button>
    </div>
    <span class="count-badge" id="countBadge">— entries</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="main">

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--s1)"></div>S1 = Edgar Cayce</div>
    <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--s2)"></div>S2 = Sarah Breskman Cosme</div>
    <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--s3)"></div>S3 = Bashar / Darryl Anka</div>
    <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--c3)"></div>★★★ = 3-source corroboration</div>
    <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--c2)"></div>★★ = 2-source corroboration</div>
    <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--c1)"></div>★ = Partial / thematic only</div>
    <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--c0)"></div>○ = Single source unique claim</div>
  </div>

  <div id="noResults" class="no-results">No entries match your search.</div>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <!-- CATEGORY 1: CHRONOLOGY -->
  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="category-section" data-category="chronology">
    <div class="category-header">
      <span class="category-label">01 — Chronology &amp; Phases</span>
      <span class="category-count" id="count-chronology"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s1 s3" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Three distinct phases / civilisations</strong> — Atlantis existed in three separate phases, each rising to a peak and ending catastrophically.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s1">S1 Cayce</span><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">Three destructions explicitly described across readings</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S2 Cosme</span><span class="detail-val" style="color:var(--text3)">Not explicitly stated as three phases</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val agree">Confirms three phases; validates Lazaris's timeline (~65,000 BCE to ~12,800 BCE)</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s1 s3" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Final destruction date ~10,600–12,800 BCE</strong> — The last Atlantean landmasses were destroyed in a single catastrophic event.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s1">S1 Cayce</span><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">~10,600 BCE ("before the Prince of Peace")</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S2 Cosme</span><span class="detail-val" style="color:var(--text3)">No precise date given</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">~12,800 years ago / ~10,800 BCE. Slight divergence from Cayce (~2,200 years)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-row">Note: Bashar's date aligns with the Younger Dryas Impact Hypothesis (~12,800 BP). Cayce's date is earlier. Both point to the same general era.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s1 s3" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>First phase began ~65,000 years ago</strong> — Earliest Atlantean civilisation was extremely ancient.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s1">S1 Cayce</span><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">~200,000 BCE for Amilius/earliest Atlanteans (ambiguous — "light years" caveat)</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">First phase ~65,000 BCE; prime/height at 20,000–30,000 BCE</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s1 s2" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Lemuria / Mu destroyed before Atlantis</strong> — A separate South Pacific civilisation was destroyed prior to the final Atlantean destruction.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s1">S1 Cayce</span><span class="pill pill-s2">S2 Cosme</span><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">Lemuria mentioned briefly; already gone by ~10,700 BCE</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S2 Cosme</span><span class="detail-val">Lymuria/Amun destroyed ~25,000 years ago by deliberate Atlantean tidal wave attack</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">Mu destruction = natural cycles (volcanic/earthquake). Not caused by Atlantis. Diverges from Cosme on mechanism.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-row">Structural divergence: Cosme says Atlantis deliberately destroyed Lemuria. Bashar says natural cycles. Cayce is silent on mechanism.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s3" data-corr="0">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-0">○</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Halloween / All Souls Day = anniversary of Atlantis destruction</strong> — October 31–November 2 originally commemorated the day before, day of, and day after Atlantis was destroyed.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="note-row">Unique to Bashar (B3). Not mentioned in Cayce or Cosme. Highly specific and culturally testable claim.</div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <!-- CATEGORY 2: GEOGRAPHY & LOCATION -->
  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="category-section" data-category="geography">
    <div class="category-header">
      <span class="category-label">02 — Geography &amp; Location</span>
      <span class="category-count" id="count-geography"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s1 s3" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Atlantis located in the Atlantic Ocean</strong> — Main landmass was in what is now the Atlantic, between the Americas and Europe/Africa.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s1">S1 Cayce</span><span class="pill pill-s2">S2 Cosme</span><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">Between Gulf of Mexico and Mediterranean Sea; size of Europe + Asia</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S2 Cosme</span><span class="detail-val">Island in Atlantic (implied); Atlanteans distinct from South Pacific Lymurians</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">Central seat = Bahamas, Cuba, Florida area. Several hundred thousand sq miles originally.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s3" data-corr="0">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-0">○</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Bahamas and Cuba = submerged core of Atlantis</strong> — The Bahamas/Grand Bahama Banks and Cuba were the main islands of Atlantis, now submerged because ocean levels rose 250–300 feet after ice melt.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">Poseidia near Bimini (consistent but less specific)</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">Explicit: Bahamas, Cuba, parts of Florida. Ocean floor maps show original outlines.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s2 s3" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Lemuria / Mu located in South Pacific</strong> — A separate civilisation existed on South Pacific landmasses now submerged.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s2">S2 Cosme</span><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S2 Cosme</span><span class="detail-val">South Pacific, encompassing Easter Island area, stretched toward South America</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">South Pacific land masses now submerged. Hawaii = last remnant above ocean.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s1 s3" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Empire extended globally</strong> — Atlantean influence reached North/Central/South America, Africa, Mediterranean, Europe, and Asia.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s1">S1 Cayce</span><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">Migrations to Pyrenees, Og/Peru, Yucatan, Egypt, Mound Builder region</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">Influence extended into N/C/S America, Africa, Mediterranean, Europe, Asian subcontinent</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s3" data-corr="0">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-0">○</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Bimini Road = collapsed wall, not a road</strong> — The underwater Bimini Road formation is a collapsed wall from a building, not a road. Visible because ocean levels were 250–300 feet lower during Atlantean times.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val">Submerged temples near Bimini = records repository</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val conflict">Contradicts Cayce: Bimini Road built AFTER Atlantis (within 5,000 years of destruction) by people drawn to residual energy</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s3" data-corr="0">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-0">○</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Underwater structures confirmed off western Cuba</strong> — A definitively confirmed Atlantean outpost has been discovered off the western tip of Cuba, known to a small group of scientists.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="note-row">Potentially references the 2001 Paulina Zelitsky / ADC expedition findings off western Cuba. Archaeologically testable.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s1 s3" data-corr="2">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-2">★★</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Knossos / Minoan civilisation = Atlantean colony</strong> — The Temple of Knossos on Crete is an Atlantean colony and preserves Atlantean cultural elements.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S3 Bashar</span><span class="detail-val">Temple of Knossos = Atlantean colony. Labyrinth = initiation practice from Atlantis. Crystals buried at each labyrinth turn. Atlanteans were bull worshippers — hence Minotaur legend. Pillars: red and black. Minoan Linear A = derivative of Atlantean script.</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val" style="color:var(--text3)">Not mentioned specifically</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-row">Crystals buried at each turn of the Knossos labyrinth is an archaeologically specific and testable claim.</div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <!-- CATEGORY 3: DESTRUCTION MECHANISM -->
  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="category-section" data-category="destruction">
    <div class="category-header">
      <span class="category-label">03 — Destruction Mechanism</span>
      <span class="category-count" id="count-destruction"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="entry" data-sources="s3" data-corr="0">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <div class="corr-badge corr-0">○</div>
        <div class="entry-claim"><strong>Comet impact in Atlantic Ocean</strong> — A large master comet entered eccentric orbit, bombarded Earth twice per year for over two decades, then the primary body struck the Atlantic Ocean causing 300-foot tsunamis.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-pills"><span class="pill pill-s3">S3 Bashar</span></div>
      <div class="detail-row">
        <span class="detail-label">S1 Cayce</span><span class="detail-val conflict">Volcanic/geological upheaval from crystal misuse (Firestone tuned too high)</span>
        <span class="detail-label">S2 Cosme</span><span class="detail-val conflict">Deliberate sabotage — prisoner fed wrong crystal calculations; bomb misfired</span>
